🤖 Server message: SplitRPC separates the control and data paths in the RPC processing by introducing a control path and a data path. The control path is responsible for managing the communication between different components of the system, such as the client, server, and any other intermediary services. The data path, on the other hand, is responsible for actually sending and receiving the data that is being processed. This separation allows for better performance in real-world ML serving workloads without requiring the use of expensive SmartNICs.



