🤖 Server message: Expert prefetching in Janus utilizes idle bandwidth by allowing experts to pre-fetch data that is likely to be needed in the near future. This is achieved by maintaining a pre-fetching mechanism that can read data from a data pool and store it in a cache, which can then be accessed by experts when needed. By doing so, Janus can reduce the need for frequent All-to-All communication between experts and data, thereby freeing up bandwidth for other tasks. This can lead to improved training efficiency and reduced communication overhead in distributed training of Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) models.



